quran[14]{c,v,t}:
  106,1,"(He did this) to make the Quraysh feel secure,"
  106,2,secure in their trading journeys of winter and summer.*
  106,3,"So let them worship the Lord of this House,"
  106,4,Who has fed them (by relieving them) from hunger and secured them from fear.
  107,1,Have you seen the one who denies faith?*
  107,2,"That is the one who repulses the orphan,"
  107,3,and does not urge the feeding of the needy.
  107,4,"So ruined are the ones who pray,"
  107,5,"who are heedless of their prayers,"
  107,6,"those who only strive to be seen (by the people),"
  107,7,but deny (even the simplest of) aid in daily necessities.
  108,1,"(O Prophet!) Indeed, We have granted you an infinite abundance of goodness.*"
  108,2,So pray to your Lord and offer sacrifice.
  108,3,"Indeed, your enemy shall be the one without posterity. (Or: indeed, your enemy shall be the one cut off from all goodness.)"
